course: dictionary
lesson: 15970
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Unwind is one of them. The words around it give you the clue. «I unwind by reading after school.» Reading is a way to rest, so unwind means to relax.
explain: Now read this: «Dad unwound the hosepipe so we could water the garden.» Nothing here is about resting. A hosepipe is kept rolled up, and to unwind it is to undo the roll so it lies out straight. Ask yourself which meaning fits: relax, or undo the roll? The hosepipe points to undo.
explain: Unwind is a verb, so its form changes: I unwind today, I unwound yesterday, and I have unwound before. Add -ing for unwinding. Use the sentence and the verb form together to find the right meaning.
fact: «Unwind» means to relax after being busy, tired or worried.
fact: «Unwind» can also mean to undo something from a roll or coil, like wool or a hosepipe.
fact: Other ways to unwind include sport, music, reading and time outdoors.
fact: The past tense of unwind is «unwound».
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «After a busy day, I unwind with a book.» What does unwind mean here? | To shout loudly | To wind something tighter | *To relax | To run very fast
exercise: «Grandma unwound the wool so the cat could play.» What does unwound mean? | To knit a hat | To sell the wool | *To undo a coil of wool | To tie a knot
exercise: What is the past tense of unwind? | unwinded | unwinding | *unwound | unwinds
test: «Mum likes to unwind in the bath after work.» What does unwind mean? | To undo a rope | To shout | To hurry | *To relax
test: «Tom unwound the hosepipe across the lawn.» What is the best meaning of unwound? | *Undid the roll so it lay straight | To wash | To pack away | To tangle
exam: Which sentence uses unwind to mean relax? | «The hose was unwound and wet.» | «He wound the wire tight.» | *«She unwinds with music after school.» | «She unwound the string from the reel.»
